<title>ITALY: Italy's Naples sees November CPI at 2.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Naples sees November CPI at 2.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>NAPLES, Italy 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Naples said its November consumer price index stood at 2.9 percent month-on-month and 0.3 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In October, the Naples inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 3.2 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Naples is one of 10 Italian cities which published inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.64 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to October 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.3   (0.2)     2.9 (3.2)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.0  (-0.1)     3.9 (4.1)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.3   (0.5)     1.9 (1.6)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.9   (0.8)     2.0 (1.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.1   (0.2)     0.8 (1.8)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0   (0.1)     1.3 (1.3)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.8  (-0.1)     6.4 (8.5)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.6   (0.0)     4.1 (3.7)</p>
<p>    Education			   2.0   (0.7)     1.7 (-0.3)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.4   (0.2)     3.1 (2.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0  (-0.2)     1.6 (1.8)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
